{"id":470141,"title":"More descriptive grouped task indicator","line":"Grouped tasks in the task manager now show a small arrow pointing away from the panel instead of a plus, so they no longer look like an \"add\" button.","kind":"wish","status":"fixed","repos":["libplasma"],"date":"2026-11-24","explanation":"The Breeze Plasma theme marks a task that groups several windows with a small accent-coloured badge holding a plus sign. The colour was already changed from green to the accent colour in 2024, but the plus still reads as \"add\" or \"create\" and doesn't hint that more windows sit behind the icon. The change keeps the same badge, size and colours and replaces the plus with a chevron pointing away from the panel edge (up on a bottom panel, down on a top one, sideways on side panels), the usual cue for something that expands. It is a theme-only change in Breeze's widgets/tasks.svg; the task manager code and third-party themes are untouched.","commits":[{"repo":"libplasma","message":"Breeze theme: Show an arrow instead of a plus on grouped tasks\n\nThe plus on grouped tasks reads as \"add\" or \"create something new\" and\nsays nothing about the windows hidden behind the icon. Draw a chevron\npointing away from the panel edge, hinting that the group can expand.\n\nBUG: 470141"}],"patches":[{"repo":"libplasma","diff":"diff --git a/src/desktoptheme/breeze/widgets/tasks.svg b/src/desktoptheme/breeze/widgets/tasks.svg\nindex c60707355..5c493132d 100644\n--- a/src/desktoptheme/breeze/widgets/tasks.svg\n+++ b/src/desktoptheme/breeze/widgets/tasks.svg\n@@ -953,26 +953,26 @@\n     <g id=\"group-expander-bottom\" transform=\"matrix(1.2222222 0 0 1.2222222 -97 -16.777778)\">\n         <path id=\"path4927\" d=\"m211.5 89.000002a4.4999957 4.5000003 0 0 0-4.5 4.5 4.4999957 4.5000003 0 0 0 4.5 4.5 4.4999957 4.5000003 0 0 0 4.5-4.5 4.4999957 4.5000003 0 0 0-4.5-4.5z\" opacity=\".25\"/>\n         <path id=\"path4931\" class=\"ColorScheme-ButtonFocus\" d=\"m211.50001 89.818184a3.